      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdint>\n#ifdef __ARM_NEON\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    \n    // Flattened prefix-sum array with an extra row/column of zeros.\n    const int stride = n + 1;\n    std::vector<int64_t> ps(stride * stride, 0);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int val;\n            scanf(\"%d\", &val);\n            row_sum += val;\n            ps[(i + 1) * stride + (j + 1)] = ps[i * stride + (j + 1)] + row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    assert(s < n && s > 0 && n > 0);\n    \n    int64_t mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    const int jmax = n - s;\n    \n#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        const int base_i   = i * stride;\n        const int base_is  = (i + s) * stride;\n        \n#ifdef __ARM_NEON\n        // Process two consecutive columns at once using NEON.\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 1 <= jmax; j += 2) {\n            const int64x2_t v_a = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_is + (j + s)]);\n            const int64x2_t v_b = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_i  + (j + s)]);\n            const int64x2_t v_c = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_is + j]);\n            const int64x2_t v_d = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_i  + j]);\n            \n            int64x2_t sum = vsubq_s64(v_a, v_b);\n            sum = vsubq_s64(sum, v_c);\n            sum = vaddq_s64(sum, v_d);\n            \n            const int64_t s0 = vgetq_lane_s64(sum, 0);\n            const int64_t s1 = vgetq_lane_s64(sum, 1);\n            if (s0 > mxSum) mxSum = s0;\n            if (s1 > mxSum) mxSum = s1;\n        }\n        // Handle remaining column.\n        for (; j <= jmax; ++j) {\n#else\n        // Scalar fallback (auto-vectorized by compiler).\n        for (int j = 0; j <= jmax; ++j) {\n#endif\n            const int64_t sum_val = ps[base_is + (j + s)] - ps[base_i + (j + s)] \n                                  - ps[base_is + j] + ps[base_i + j];\n            if (sum_val > mxSum) mxSum = sum_val;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", static_cast<long long>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combine the integral-image (prefix-sum) algorithm with explicit ARM NEON SIMD intrinsics to compute two submatrix sums simultaneously, halving the inner-loop iterations. The flattened prefix array enables contiguous vector loads; OpenMP parallelizes over rows while reduction(max:mxSum) remains correct. This approach eliminates all loop-carried dependencies and fully exploits both ILP and thread-level parallelism on ARM64.",
  "notes": "Fixed previous NEON compilation errors by using int64_t (from <cstdint>) instead of long long, including <climits> for LLONG_MIN, and flattening the prefix-sum array to a single contiguous vector. The code conditionally uses intrinsics only when __ARM_NEON is defined; otherwise falls back to scalar loops that the compiler can auto-vectorize.",
